{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-28", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves (35 mm, KODAK PROFESSIONAL T-MAX Developer, small tank, 20 C, diffuse visual, 6/7/10/12 min) and spectral sensitivity (D=1.0 above D-min, Developer D-76) digitised from the Kodak data sheet F-4001 (KODAK PROFESSIONAL T-MAX P3200 Film, March 2018). Reference speed per curve from the sheet's T-MAX development table (20 C): 12 min = EI 3200, 10 min = EI 1131 (interpolated between EI 800 and 1600), 7 min = EI 200 (below the table, clamped); the sheet's nominal speed is EI 1000 in T-MAX Developer (EI 800 rounded). Mid-grey exposure is anchored at log10(14.5/EI) for each curve. 6 min curve (pull) omitted so that the default family entry is 10 min. Original data are property of Eastman Kodak Company. Exposure axis shifted per curve as described above (0 = mid-grey exposure at that curve's reference speed); sensitivity offset chosen so that mid-grey renders at the reference level. Tail above the sheet range extrapolated with decaying slope. Derived from spektrafilm profile format; modified by graineo (see modifications).", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; no spektrafilm measurement data reused except the profile format and wavelength grid. grain_scale set so that simulated RMS granularity (density 1.0, 48 um aperture) matches the data sheet value 18."}, "info": {"grain_size_classes": {"classes": 4, "area_spread": 2.0, "speed_exponent": 1.0}, "stock": "kodak_tmax_p3200", "name": "Kodak T-MAX P3200 Professional Negative Film (TMZ), T-MAX developer", "type": "negative", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "strong", "target_print": null, "channel_model": "bw", "densitometer": "diffuse_visual", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "grain_scale": 0.922, "default_look": {"film_dev": 12.0, "paper_grade": 2.0, "grain": 1.1, "print_ev": -0.1, "paper": "ilford_multigrade_iv_rc", "taking_filter": "gruen11", "taking_filter_amount": 0.5}, "card": {"maker": "Kodak", "iso": 3200, "type": "Schwarzwei\u00dfnegativfilm (T-Korn, hochempfindlich)", "rms": 18, "additional": "Datenblatt F-4001", "text": "F\u00fcr wenig Licht: weiches, deutliches Korn und flacherer Kontrast in den Schatten. Die Empfindlichkeit h\u00e4ngt stark von der Entwicklungszeit ab (EI 800 bis 3200 und mehr).", "source": "Kodak F-4001", "process": "Schwarzwei\u00df-Negativentwicklung (verl\u00e4ngert)", "period": "2012 eingestellt, seit M\u00e4rz 2018 wieder erh\u00e4ltlich", "suitable": ["Nachtaufnahmen aus der Hand", "Sport und Action bei wenig Licht", "Teleaufnahmen bei D\u00e4mmerung"], "less_suitable": ["feine Vergr\u00f6\u00dferungen", "Studio und Landschaft"], "tips": ["Aufnahmefilter Gr\u00fcn (11): Der Look \u201eAbgestimmt\u201c legt ihn bereits mit etwa 50 % davor (Haut beh\u00e4lt Tiefe, Laub wird heller); \u201eKeiner\u201c oder \u201eDatenblatt\u201c zeigt die rohe Wiedergabe.", "Entwicklungszeit 7, 10 oder 12 Minuten: je l\u00e4nger, desto mehr Empfindlichkeit, Kontrast und Korn (Standard im abgestimmten Look: 12 Minuten, Papiergrad 2)."], "facts": [{"text": "Der Film ist mit 3200 beschriftet, hat aber nur etwa 800 bis 1000 Nennempfindlichkeit und ist f\u00fcr Push-Entwicklung gedacht (nutzbar von EI 1600 bis 25000). Kodak stellte ihn am 1. Oktober 2012 wegen hoher Herstellkosten ein und k\u00fcndigte am 23. Februar 2018 die R\u00fcckkehr an.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kodak_T-MAX"}, {"text": "Das Datenblatt von M\u00e4rz 2018 nennt T-Grain-Emulsion, hohe bis ultrahohe Empfindlichkeit und feineres Korn als andere schnelle Schwarzwei\u00dffilme; wegen der Empfindlichkeit r\u00e4t Kodak am Flughafen zur Handkontrolle.", "source": "Kodak F-4001 (M\u00e4rz 2018)"}]}}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725.0, 730.0, 735.0, 740.0, 745.0, 750.0, 755.0, 760.0, 765.0, 770.0, 775.0, 780.0], "log_sensitivity": [[null], [null], [null], [null], [null], [-0.5656750579718808], [-0.5745688775409539], [-0.5942914975960738], [-0.6173343128900417], [-0.6397470077796383], [-0.6614162162442226], [-0.6820630775665528], [-0.7017066095949878], [-0.7221483052292955], [-0.7463487141427634], [-0.7759522789835007], [-0.8096124161901388], [-0.8453964642560972], [-0.8814580299381727], [-0.9193185754479749], [-0.9576258508334662], [-0.9936618529380359], [-1.0232907368685678], [-1.044205208178295], [-1.053450283099255], [-1.0520765011528266], [-1.042893973952888], [-1.0288237334230133], [-1.0105624955838122], [-0.9912593256903194], [-0.9740707845550393], [-0.9640743269540298], [-0.9598869180035385], [-0.9546918155908458], [-0.9560933401210883], [-0.97135596323325], [-0.9946398599311718], [-1.0147385368253254], [-1.0294135496081733], [-1.0402979